All 15 tests pass. Here's what was fixed:

**`src/auth.py`:**
- `has_permission`: case-insensitive comparison was missing — now lowers both sides
- `is_admin_or_owner`: used `and` instead of `or` — admin *or* owner should grant access

**`src/inventory.py`:**
- `__init__`: mutable default `{}` was shared across instances — now uses `None` default with `dict(initial)` copy
- `add`: overwrote quantity instead of accumulating — now uses `+=`
- `reserve`: used `>=` instead of `>` — reserving exactly the available stock is valid
- `release`: no guard against releasing more than reserved — now raises `ValueError`

**`src/text_utils.py`:**
- `slugify`: didn't lowercase alphanumerics — now calls `.lower()` on each char
- `slugify`: single `replace("--","-")` missed longer runs like `---` — replaced with `re.sub(r"-+", "-", ...)`
- `truncate`: didn't subtract suffix length from truncation point — now uses `text[:max_len - len(suffix)] + suffix`
